<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Titlis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mount Titlis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Titlis is a mountain of the Uri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, rising to 3,238 metres on the border of the cantons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obwalden">Obwalden</a> and Bern. It overlooks the valley and abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/engelberg">Engelberg</a>, founded below it in 1120. Its glacier and summit are reached by cable cars from Engelberg, including the world's first revolving cable car, opened in 1992.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/titlis.jpg" alt="Titlis" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CARLO FEDELE BARRI · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Titlis_W.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
